# Castle Wall daemon Rust artifacts
castle-wall-daemon/target/

# Local pre-commit hook transcripts. The commit hook runs the whole suite and
# its log is the only record of a run that took ~9 minutes, so keep it beside
# the worktree rather than in a system temp dir that a reboot deletes. It is
# a local artifact and must never be committed: the repo-root allowlist guard
# (server/test/structure/root-allowlist.test.ts) fails the suite if it is.
.hooklogs/

# Cargo.lock IS tracked for this crate: the Linux CI job builds with `--locked`,
# which fails outright without a committed lock, and the MSRV job's whole point is
# that the exact resolved graph still builds on Rust 1.75. It was ignored while the
# crate was a scratch prototype; do not re-add an ignore line for it.

# Castle Wall macOS Swift package artifacts
castle-wall-macos/.build/
castle-wall-macos/build/
castle-wall-macos/Package.resolved

# Castle Wall VMM Swift package artifacts (split out of castle-wall-macos)
castle-wall-vmm/.build/
castle-wall-vmm/build/
castle-wall-vmm/Package.resolved

# Per-machine Claude Code permissions; never commit
.claude/settings.local.json

# dev-scratch PR-prep notes do not belong in the repo root (professionalization 2026-06-14)
/*_HANDOFF.md
/*_PR_BODY.md

# macOS/iCloud duplication artifacts, e.g. "settings.local 2.json" (gh-hygiene 2026-06-16)
* [0-9].json
* [0-9].md

.test-baseline-overrides.log
# Written into the repo root by scripts/verify-fail-before.sh whenever a run
# records an exemption or a SKIP_FAIL_BEFORE override. Local runs left it as an
# untracked file one `git add .` away from being committed.
.fail-before-overrides.log

# Marker written by the vitest globalSetup for the duration of a run; the
# credential chokepoint reads it so a child spawned with a scrubbed env still
# knows it belongs to the test run. See server/test/setup/test-run-marker.ts.
server/.sanctuary-test-run
